{"authored" [{"question" "q-122342" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A particle $P$ moves along the $x$-axis in the direction of increasing $x,$ away from a fixed origin $O.$ When the displacement of $P$ from $O$ is $x\\,m,$ its velocity is $v\\,m/s$ and its acceleration is $(4{x}^{3}+4x)\\,{m/s}^{2}.$ If $v=\\sqrt{6}\\,m/s$ when $x=1\\,\\text{m},$ find the velocity of $P$ when $x=2\\,\\text{m}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042763/state.json" "file_sha256" "da9200e531b3ab7444cb5a4c08c9cf15199728fb4376cbd0f00077184e7aa70d" "basis" 1577 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042763/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-122342" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042763/assets/4e0b8b816ca3b86fa90ea785df1308f53a4763baa2c2aa2192b9d7bfa0259855.png)\n\nSince the acceleration of the particle $P$ is $(4{x}^{3}+4x)\\,{m/s}^{2},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}=4{x}^{3}+4x.\n$$\n\nUsing the fact that \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{1}{2}{v}^{2})\n$$\n\nwe can rewrite our equation as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{1}{2}{v}^{2})=4{x}^{3}+4x.\n$$\n\nIntegrating both sides of the above equation with respect to $x,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{1}{2}{v}^{2})\\text{d}x & =\\int (4{x}^{3}+4x)\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives the general solution\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}{v}^{2}={x}^{4}+2{x}^{2}+C.\n$$\n\nNow, since $v=\\sqrt{6}\\,m/s$ when $x=1\\,\\text{m},$ we can find the value of the constant $C$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}(\\sqrt{6})^{2} & ={1}^{4}+2(1)^{2}+C \\\\ 3 & =3+C \\\\ C & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}{v}^{2} & ={x}^{4}+2{x}^{2} \\\\ {v}^{2} & =2({x}^{4}+2{x}^{2}) \\\\ v & =\\pm \\sqrt{2({x}^{4}+2{x}^{2})}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the particle is moving in the direction of increasing $x,$ we have that $v(x)>0,$ so we can discard the negative square root. Therefore,\n\n$$\nv=\\sqrt{2({x}^{4}+2{x}^{2})}.\n$$\n\nFinally, the velocity of $P$ at $x=2$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\sqrt{2({2}^{4}+2(2)^{2})} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{48} \\\\  & =4\\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{m/s}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042763/state.json" "file_sha256" "da9200e531b3ab7444cb5a4c08c9cf15199728fb4376cbd0f00077184e7aa70d" "basis" 1577 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042763/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-122342" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042763/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "785f7610edd208db81cfb7c4ec13a140b5ce47e04ba0e053de3c67f7552cdd94" "basis" 1577 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042763/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-122342" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042763/state.json" "file_sha256" "da9200e531b3ab7444cb5a4c08c9cf15199728fb4376cbd0f00077184e7aa70d" "basis" 1577 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042763/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-122342" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "2\\sqrt{6}\\,\\text{m/s}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042763/state.json" "file_sha256" "da9200e531b3ab7444cb5a4c08c9cf15199728fb4376cbd0f00077184e7aa70d" "basis" 1577 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042763/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-122342" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "3\\sqrt{2}\\,\\text{m/s}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042763/state.json" "file_sha256" "da9200e531b3ab7444cb5a4c08c9cf15199728fb4376cbd0f00077184e7aa70d" "basis" 1577 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042763/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-122342" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "4\\,\\text{m/s}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042763/state.json" "file_sha256" "da9200e531b3ab7444cb5a4c08c9cf15199728fb4376cbd0f00077184e7aa70d" "basis" 1577 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042763/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-122342" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "4\\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{m/s}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042763/state.json" "file_sha256" "da9200e531b3ab7444cb5a4c08c9cf15199728fb4376cbd0f00077184e7aa70d" "basis" 1577 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042763/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-122342" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "5\\,\\text{m/s}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042763/state.json" "file_sha256" "da9200e531b3ab7444cb5a4c08c9cf15199728fb4376cbd0f00077184e7aa70d" "basis" 1577 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042763/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-122339" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A particle $P$ moves along the $x$-axis in the direction of decreasing $x$ where $x>0.$ When the displacement of $P$ from the origin $O$ is $x\\,m,$ its velocity is $v\\,m/s$ and its acceleration is $\\frac{1}{16}x\\,{m/s}^{2}.$ If $P$ has a displacement of $0\\,m$ when its velocity is $-2\\,m/s,$ find $v$ in terms of $x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042763/state.json" "file_sha256" "da9200e531b3ab7444cb5a4c08c9cf15199728fb4376cbd0f00077184e7aa70d" "basis" 1577 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042763/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-122339" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042763/assets/ba6a85da04d9ba03bcdba9b938dac208a770933310cd25c19bf0ec3e19ef17c7.png)\n\nSince the acceleration of the particle $P$ is $\\frac{1}{16}x\\,{m/s}^{2},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{1}{16}x.\n$$\n\nUsing the fact that \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{1}{2}{v}^{2}),\n$$\n\nwe can rewrite our equation as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{1}{2}{v}^{2})=\\frac{1}{16}x.\n$$\n\nIntegrating both sides of the above equation with respect to $x,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{1}{2}{v}^{2})\\text{d}x=\\int (\\frac{1}{16}x)\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nwhich gives the general solution\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}{v}^{2}=\\frac{1}{32}{x}^{2}+C.\n$$\n\nNow, since $x=0\\,\\text{m}$ when $v=-2\\,\\text{m/s},$ we can find the value of the constant $C$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}{v}^{2} & =\\frac{1}{32}{x}^{2}+C \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}(-2)^{2} & =\\frac{1}{32}(0)^{2}+C \\\\ 2 & =0+C \\\\ C & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}{v}^{2} & =\\frac{1}{32}{x}^{2}+2 \\\\ {v}^{2} & =\\frac{1}{16}{x}^{2}+4 \\\\ {v}^{2} & =\\frac{1}{16}({x}^{2}+64) \\\\ v & =\\pm \\frac{1}{4}\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+64}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since the particle is moving in the direction of decreasing  $x,$ we have that $v(x)<0,$ so we can discard the positive square root. Therefore,\n\n$$\nv(x)=-\\frac{1}{4}\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+64}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042763/state.json" "file_sha256" "da9200e531b3ab7444cb5a4c08c9cf15199728fb4376cbd0f00077184e7aa70d" "basis" 1577 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042763/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-122339" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042763/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "785f7610edd208db81cfb7c4ec13a140b5ce47e04ba0e053de3c67f7552cdd94" "basis" 1577 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042763/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-122339" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042763/state.json" "file_sha256" "da9200e531b3ab7444cb5a4c08c9cf15199728fb4376cbd0f00077184e7aa70d" "basis" 1577 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042763/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-122339" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "v(x)=-\\frac{1}{2}\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+16}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042763/state.json" "file_sha256" "da9200e531b3ab7444cb5a4c08c9cf15199728fb4376cbd0f00077184e7aa70d" "basis" 1577 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042763/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-122339" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "v(x)=-\\frac{1}{4}\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+64}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042763/state.json" "file_sha256" "da9200e531b3ab7444cb5a4c08c9cf15199728fb4376cbd0f00077184e7aa70d" "basis" 1577 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042763/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-122339" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "v(x)=-\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+4}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042763/state.json" "file_sha256" "da9200e531b3ab7444cb5a4c08c9cf15199728fb4376cbd0f00077184e7aa70d" "basis" 1577 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042763/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "